======================================================================
PHASE 2 — DELIVERABLE 2: TEST-SET CALIBRATION QUALITY
======================================================================

Methodology:
  Calibration was fitted on the VALIDATION set (Platt scaling).
  This report evaluates calibration quality on the held-out TEST set.
  ECE and MCE are computed with 15 equal-width probability bins.
  Brier score is the reference scalar for overall calibration quality.

  ECE = Expected Calibration Error = sum_b (n_b/N) * |acc_b - conf_b|
  MCE = Maximum Calibration Error  = max_b |acc_b - conf_b|
  Lower values indicate better calibration.

  Metric                                 XGBoost   Random Forest
  ------------------------------------------------------------
  ECE (15 bins)                         0.016692        0.017362
  MCE (15 bins)                         0.077144        0.118579
  Brier Score (test)                    0.038720        0.045910

Interpretation:
  ECE < 0.02 is generally considered well-calibrated for financial models.
  See calibration_quality_test.png for reliability diagrams.
