PHASE 2 — DELIVERABLE 5: TEMPORAL COHORT PERFORMANCE
======================================================================

IMPORTANT LIMITATION:
  This analysis evaluates performance across origination-year cohorts
  WITHIN the existing 2007-2018 LendingClub dataset. It is a temporal
  robustness proxy only. No post-2018 data exists on this machine.
  These results do NOT support conclusions about post-2018 generalization.

Methodology:
  Test set rows are assigned to cohorts by their issue_d origination year.
  Row alignment: test.parquet (issue_d) joined to test_preprocessed.parquet
  by position — both preserve the temporal sort order from Phase 1 split.
  Minimum cohort size: 200 loans.

    Year        N  DefRate   ROC-AUC    PR-AUC     Brier
  ----------------------------------------------------
    2017  145,486    0.232    0.9736    0.9328  0.041649
    2018   56,318    0.158    0.9716    0.9258  0.031155

Interpretation:
  A declining PR-AUC trend toward recent years would suggest the model
  is less accurate on later loans, consistent with concept drift.
  Stable or improving metrics indicate within-period robustness.
  This cannot substitute for true out-of-period evaluation.
