PHASE 2 — DELIVERABLE 1: LAST-FICO LEAKAGE INVESTIGATION
======================================================================

BACKGROUND:
  last_fico_range_low + last_fico_range_high account for
  64.3% of Phase 1 XGBoost feature importance.
  The feature audit flagged both as 'manual review recommended'.
  The LendingClub data dictionary is NOT available in this repository.
  This investigation uses empirical evidence only.

CORRELATION EVIDENCE (training set — Pearson):
  last_fico_range_low_vs_fico_range_low: 0.2439
  last_fico_range_low_vs_fico_range_high: 0.2439
  last_fico_range_high_vs_fico_range_low: 0.3311
  last_fico_range_high_vs_fico_range_high: 0.3311

DRIFT EVIDENCE (last_fico_low - fico_low on training set):
  Mean difference:         -33.51
  Std difference:          125.55
  Pct last == orig:        0.034
  Pct last < orig:         0.522
  Pct last > orig:         0.443

  Interpretation: If pct_last_eq_orig is high (>0.70), last_fico is
  likely the origination-time pull (same as fico). If low and std is
  large, post-origination drift is more likely.

VARIANT MODEL COMPARISON (test set, calibrated, threshold=0.50):
  Metric             Phase 1 XGB    No-LastFico    Delta
  ------------------------------------------------------
  ROC-AUC                 0.9736         0.7164  -0.2572
  PR-AUC                  0.9315         0.3927  -0.5388
  Brier                 0.038720       0.150958

VERDICT: HIGH CONCERN: last_fico shows significant drift from fico. Consistent with post-origination credit pulls.

CAVEAT: Official LendingClub data dictionary not available in this repository. Conclusion is based on empirical evidence only and is not definitive. The data dictionary should be consulted before drawing final conclusions.
