PHASE 2 CONCLUSIONS AND PHASE 3 RECOMMENDATIONS
??????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????

  PRIMARY MODEL FOR PHASE 3:
    Calibrated XGBoost (Phase 1) remains the recommended model unless the
    leakage investigation concludes last_fico is post-origination (HIGH CONCERN
    verdict). In that case, the no-last-fico variant should be used for Phase 3.

  LAST-FICO DECISION RULE:
    If leakage verdict is LOW CONCERN:  use Phase 1 calibrated XGBoost.
    If leakage verdict is HIGH CONCERN: use xgboost_nolastfico_calibrated.pkl.
    The official LendingClub data dictionary should confirm this before Phase 3.

  JOINT APPLICATIONS IN PHASE 3:
    The Phase 3 counterfactual engine should note that joint application
    features (annual_inc_joint, dti_joint, sec_app_fico) are only populated
    for joint loans. Phase 3 must handle individual loans correctly regardless
    of joint-field values (already true via Phase 1 median imputation).

  GRADE IN PHASE 3:
    Grade/sub_grade are treated as fixed (non-actionable) in Phase 3.
    int_rate_spread is derived from grade and is also non-actionable.
    The grade-free variant delta informs how much information Phase 3 loses
    if grade becomes unavailable.

